                "The Drain of Wealth Theory: Demonstrating that Britain extracted a unilateral unrequited transfer of Indian national wealth (Home Charges, guaranteed interest on railways, pensions, profits of foreign banks and shipping companies) amounting to roughly 2 to 3 percent of India's national income annually, suffocating domestic capital formation.",
                "De-industrialisation and Peasantisation: Showing how one-way free trade and tariff manipulation flooded India with Lancashire textiles, destroying urban artisanal handicraft centers (Dhaka, Murshidabad, Surat) and forcing millions of unemployed weavers back into agriculture, leading to acute fragmentation of holdings and recurring catastrophic famines."
