                "The Revisionist View: Revisionist historians (Muzaffar Alam, C.A. Bayly, Sanjay Subrahmanyam, Burton Stein) demonstrated that the decline of the Delhi imperial court did not mean total economic collapse; rather, it witnessed vibrant regional political economies in successor states (Awadh, Bengal, Hyderabad, Mysore, Maratha confederacy).",
